From: Project Bluefin <no-reply@projectbluefin.io>
Subject: [PATCH] cli: tolerate a missing /proc when joining the host IPC namespace

join_host_ipc_namespace() already intends to be a no-op in restricted build
environments -- its own comment says it is "skipped when /proc/1/ns/ipc is not
accessible, which can happen in restricted build environments (e.g.
Tekton/Buildah containers) where /proc is masked even for processes with
CAP_SYS_ADMIN".

That skip only covers PermissionDenied. A sandbox that mounts no procfs at all
(BuildBarn's bb_runner with chrootIntoInputRoot builds an input root without
/proc) reports NotFound instead, so the call fails hard:

    error: reading /proc/1/ns/ipc: No such file or directory (os error 2)

`make install` runs the freshly built binary five times to generate shell
completions, so the whole build fails. Treat an absent /proc like a masked one:
either way there is no pid1 IPC namespace to join, which is exactly the
condition the existing skip describes.

diff --git a/crates/lib/src/cli.rs b/crates/lib/src/cli.rs
index 97b9a9e..d9dc48b 100644
--- a/crates/lib/src/cli.rs
+++ b/crates/lib/src/cli.rs
@@ -1795,7 +1795,14 @@ fn join_host_ipc_namespace() -> Result<()> {
     }
     let ns_pid1 = match std::fs::read_link("/proc/1/ns/ipc") {
         Ok(v) => v,
-        Err(e) if e.kind() == std::io::ErrorKind::PermissionDenied => {
+        // A masked /proc reports PermissionDenied; a sandbox with no procfs
+        // at all reports NotFound. Neither has a pid1 IPC namespace to join.
+        Err(e)
+            if matches!(
+                e.kind(),
+                std::io::ErrorKind::PermissionDenied | std::io::ErrorKind::NotFound
+            ) =>
+        {
             return Ok(());
         }
         Err(e) => return Err(e).context("reading /proc/1/ns/ipc"),
